{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1451928525,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxMjQ4MDIxODc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/331","origin":"github"},"title":"New helper to \"register\" a new data access possibility for the entire handle content","message":"Scenario: I published a dataset on some portal using means other than git annex. The data will be available for download in some way. We should have a helper that can alter an existing handle to register a newly available data source. Git annex can do this in a number of ways (e.g. special remotes). We should add a helper on top of this that can do things like:\n- [ ] Register a new URL for all files given a single base URL (and a simple templating/regex thingy that can construct the full per-file URL from the handle content: relative path, some hash, ...)\n- [ ] A way to register that a particular state of a handle (just the content) is available in a tarball accessible from a URL\n- [ ] Create some kind of \"dual configuration\" special remote. For example, I want to publish a handle to Github, while the files have to go elsewhere. I could use an rsync special remote to push them to a server, but I likely need a different configuration for public access (push via ssh, download via rsync daemon)","files":null}]}